{
 "finding": "PR #11 review (Codex, P2): support_margins projected the COM opposite to gravity's horizontal component. For nonzero floor slopes this misplaced the COM ground point by 2 * com_z * tan(slope) along the slope, so the toe/heel/minimum margins and com_outside_support_s of sloped trials were wrong.",
 "source": "movement_lab/sim02e.py",
 "archived_source": "corrections/margin-projection/source/sim02e.py",
 "before_sha256": "04fe0e8f24d61e8a11347e15347cdc181976f995947b7e3c359c43638fb3f531",
 "after_sha256": "3c769880520bdd06cf018093c4ff64891d01c7091cf498f4f5cf04a16eff0910",
 "edits": [
  [
   "  physically equivalent to standing on an inclined plane. Positive pitch: +x uphill.\n",
   "  physically equivalent to standing on an inclined plane. Positive pitch: the floor\n  descends toward +x.\n"
  ],
  [
   "    # Project the COM along gravity onto the floor plane z = 0.\n    c = com[:2] - g_hat[:2] * (com[2] / -g_hat[2])\n",
   "    # Project the COM along gravity onto the floor plane z = 0: com + s g_hat with s = com_z / -g_z > 0.\n    c = com[:2] + g_hat[:2] * (com[2] / -g_hat[2])\n"
  ]
 ],
 "fields": [
  "min_support_margin_m",
  "min_toe_margin_m",
  "min_heel_margin_m",
  "steady_toe_margin_m",
  "steady_heel_margin_m",
  "com_outside_support_s"
 ],
 "selection": "rows whose condition has a nonzero slope_deg",
 "unaffected": "Trial outcomes and every non-margin row field (margins never feed back into the simulation); zero-slope rows (gravity horizontal component is exactly +0.0); gates (computed from recoveries); training and its pilots (learn02e rollouts never request margins); 1B estimators, feasibility probes and the Phase 0 resimulation (no margins); replay frames (no margin fields).",
